---
/**
 * /cli — Mzizi on the command line, as it actually is today.
 *
 * Three things, in the order that matters to the language:
 *   1. `mz`, the language's compiler. Built from a checkout; no release.
 *   2. Installing components. React through `npx shadcn add`; Rust read from
 *      `/v1/rs`; `mzizi add` (both targets) in `@nyuchi/mzizi-cli` 0.6.0+.
 *   3. `fundi`, the agent CLI in the same package.
 *
 * The owner's decision (2026-09-29): the CLI is free, with no gate. Versions
 * and crate states are read at build time and dated, never typed in here.
 */
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
import {
  getComponentRecords,
  crateStatus,
  npmStatus,
  installCommand,
  builtAt,
  CANONICAL_BASE,
} from "../lib/registry";

const records = await getComponentRecords();
const rustCount = [...records.values()].filter((r) => r.rust).length;
const [crate, umbrella, serverUmbrella, cli] = await Promise.all([
  crateStatus("mzizi-ui"),
  crateStatus("mzizi-roots"),
  crateStatus("mzizi-roots-server"),
  npmStatus("@nyuchi/mzizi-cli"),
]);

// `mzizi add` first shipped in @nyuchi/mzizi-cli 0.6.0. Whether the latest on
// npm is at least that is asked at build time, not assumed.
const INSTALLER_SINCE = "0.6.0";
const atLeast = (version: string, floor: string) => {
  const a = version.split(/[.-]/).map(Number);
  const b = floor.split(".").map(Number);
  for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
    if ((a[i] ?? 0) !== b[i]) return (a[i] ?? 0) > b[i];
  }
  return true;
};
const installerShipped = cli.state === "published" && atLeast(cli.version, INSTALLER_SINCE);

const mzCommands = [
  { cmd: "mz check <file.mz>", what: "Does it compile. Human-readable diagnostics." },
  {
    cmd: "mz check --agent <file.mz>",
    what: "The same check as NDJSON: one line per real error with an exact span, a plain-language message and a fix tagged exact or guess, then a summary line.",
  },
  {
    cmd: "mz contract <file.mz>",
    what: "Evaluates the file's contract block against its own declarations. Exits 1 if a clause does not hold, exactly as a compile error does.",
  },
  {
    cmd: "mz fix <file.mz>",
    what: "Applies every fix tagged exact in one pass, writes the file, and re-checks it.",
  },
  { cmd: "mz outline <file.mz>", what: "The interface only, as valid Mzizi: what an agent loads instead of reading the source." },
  { cmd: "mz hash <file.mz>", what: "The root hash of the content-addressed IR, and the stored node count." },
  { cmd: "mz ir <file.mz>", what: "Every IR node with its hash and structural path." },
];
---

<Site
  title="CLI"
  eyebrow="Toolchain"
  description="Mzizi on the command line: the mz compiler, installing components (React with shadcn, Rust from /v1/rs), and the agent CLI. Free, with no gate."
  lede="Free, with no gate. The compiler first, because the language is the point; then installing components; then the agent CLI."
>
  <h2 id="mz">mz, the language's compiler</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      <code>mz</code> is the binary in
      <a href="https://github.com/mzizi-dev/mzizi">mzizi-dev/mzizi</a>. There is no
      release and no published binary yet, so it is built from a checkout, with
      nothing beyond stable Rust:
    </p>
  </div>
  <code class="cmd lead">{"git clone https://github.com/mzizi-dev/mzizi.git && cd mzizi/compiler"}</code>
  <code class="cmd lead">cargo run --bin mz -- contract ../primitives/button.mz</code>

  <div class="scroller">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          mzCommands.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{c.cmd}</code></td>
              <td>{c.what}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="prose">
    Designed but not built: <code>mz refs</code>, <code>mz path</code>,
    <code>mz patch</code> and <code>mz diff</code>. Real
    captured output is on <a href="/language#trying-it">the language page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">Installing components</h2>

  <h3>Rust (Mzizi Roots)</h3>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      {rustCount} components have a Rust implementation. Each one's source is
      served at:
    </p>
  </div>
  <code class="cmd lead">curl {CANONICAL_BASE}/rs/&lt;name&gt;</code>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The document names the crate <code>mzizi-ui</code> on crates.io.{" "}
      {crate.state === "published" && <>It is published, at <code>{crate.version}</code>: <code>cargo add mzizi-ui</code>.</>}
      {umbrella.state === "published" && (
        <>
          {" "}Or take the UI umbrella, <code>mzizi-roots</code>
          (<code>{umbrella.version}</code>), which brings <code>mzizi-ui</code>
          with the tokens, brand and shell crates in one dependency:
          <code>cargo add mzizi-roots</code>.
        </>
      )}
      {serverUmbrella.state === "published" && (
        <>
          {" "}The server side is <code>mzizi-roots-server</code>
          (<code>{serverUmbrella.version}</code>).
        </>
      )}
      {
        crate.state === "absent" && (
          <>
            <strong>That crate is not on crates.io yet</strong>, so there is no{" "}
            <code>cargo add</code> that works today. Until it is published, build
            against the source from the API or from{" "}
            <a href="https://github.com/mzizi-dev/mzizi-registry/tree/main/mzizi-rs"
              ><code>mzizi-registry/mzizi-rs</code></a
            >.
          </>
        )
      }
      {crate.state === "unknown" && <>Whether it is on crates.io could not be checked when this page was built.</>}
      {" "}<code>npx shadcn add</code> cannot install a Rust document: it rejects the
      schema.
    </p>
    <p>The <a href="/components#roots">Roots list</a> shows every component with a Rust implementation.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>React</h3>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Every component's React (TSX) build installs with shadcn, from its absolute
      URL. Always the full URL: a bare name resolves against shadcn's own
      registry and installs a different component.
    </p>
  </div>
  <code class="cmd lead">npx shadcn@latest add <span class="flag">{CANONICAL_BASE}/ui/&lt;name&gt;</span></code>
  <p class="prose">For example: <code>{installCommand("button")}</code></p>

  <h3 id="mzizi-add"><code>mzizi add</code>: both targets, one command</h3>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      {
        installerShipped ? (
          <>
            <code>mzizi add &lt;name&gt;</code> ships in <code>@nyuchi/mzizi-cli</code>{" "}
            from <code>{INSTALLER_SINCE}</code> (latest on npm: <code>{cli.state === "published" && cli.version}</code>).
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <code>mzizi add &lt;name&gt;</code> ships in <code>@nyuchi/mzizi-cli</code>{" "}
            from <code>{INSTALLER_SINCE}</code>; npm could not be checked when this page was built.
          </>
        )
      }{" "}
      It detects whether a project is React or Rust (<code>--target</code>
      overrides), resolves registry dependencies by absolute URL, and refuses
      what it cannot install honestly rather than guessing. No API key and no
      sign-in.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>React:</strong> writes the TSX files and names the npm
        dependencies, as <code>npx shadcn add</code> would.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Rust:</strong> copies no <code>.rs</code> files, because a Roots
        component is a module of the <code>mzizi-ui</code> crate, not a file to
        fork. It records the crate and checks crates.io first.{" "}
        {crate.state !== "published" && (
          <>
            While <code>mzizi-ui</code> is unpublished, it exits 1 and says so: a
            Rust install is blocked on the crate, not on the tool.
          </>
        )}
      </li>
      <li><strong>Astro:</strong> refused, because the registry serves no <code>.astro</code> files.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <code class="cmd lead">npm install --save-dev @nyuchi/mzizi-cli</code>
  <code class="cmd lead">npx mzizi add button --dry-run</code>

  <h2 id="agent">The agent CLI: <code>fundi</code></h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The same package's other binary, <code>fundi</code>, reads your project off
      disk and plans a Mzizi-aligned change against the registry and skills.
      <code>explore</code> runs offline. <code>plan</code> and <code>chat</code>
      read the MCP server; without an <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>,
      <code>plan</code> hands its context to the coding agent that ran it instead
      of calling a model itself.
    </p>
    <p>
      The CLI is free, with no gate, and so is the MCP server it reads: nothing
      needs a sign-in except the Fundi tools (<code>mzizi_fundi</code> and{" "}
      <code>mzizi_report_issue</code>), which act as your console user.
      <code>fundi login</code> exists for those alone.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="provenance">
    <span>
      Rust count read from <code>{CANONICAL_BASE}/rs/&lt;name&gt;</code>; crates.io and
      npm checked when this page was built, <time datetime={builtAt}>{builtAt}</time>.
    </span>
  </p>
</Site>
